<title>USA: GE, SNECMA get $1.1 bln USAF engine order.</title>
<headline>GE, SNECMA get $1.1 bln USAF engine order.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Electric Co and the French firm SNECMA are being jointly awarded a $1.1 billion U.S. defense contract for up to 267 engines for KC-135 tanker planes and RC-135 reconnassance planes, the Air Force said.</p>
<p>The firms have been jointly producing engines for the big U.S. military jets for more than a decade and the new engines are part of a re-engining program, the Air Force said.</p>
